.TH FLUXLAND-MENU 5 "2026-10-24" "fluxland 1.1.0" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
fluxland-menu \- menu files (the Fluxbox menu format)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The root menu (right click on the desktop, or the
.B RootMenu
command), the window menu, and menus opened with
.B CustomMenu
are read from files in Fluxbox's menu format, so a Fluxbox
.I ~/.fluxbox/menu
and menus made by
.BR fluxbox-generate_menu (1)
work unchanged.
.PP
The root menu is
.I ~/.config/fluxland/menu
(or
.IR ~/.fluxbox/menu ),
or the init file's
.BR session.menuFile .
The window menu is the
.I windowmenu
file next to it when there is one (or
.BR session.screen0.windowMenu ),
otherwise a copy of Fluxbox's default.
A menu file and the files it includes are read again when they change.
.B fluxland \-\-check\-config
reports lines fluxland wouldn't use.
.SH SYNTAX
Each line is
.PP
.RS 4
.BI [ tag "] (" label ") {" command "} <" icon >
.RE
.PP
with any field but the tag left out.
Lines that don't start with
.B [
(and so the comments,
.B #
and
.BR ! )
are ignored.
A backslash before a closing bracket makes it part of the field:
.BR "(a \e) b)" .
Brackets that balance can be nested:
.BR "(vim (as root))" .
.PP
The menu starts at
.BI [begin] " (title)"
and ends at its
.BR [end] ;
lines before the
.B [begin]
are ignored.
An
.I icon
is an image file shown beside the item's label; any line can have one.
.SH ITEMS
.TP
.BI [exec] " (label) {command}"
Run a shell command.
.TP
.BI [submenu] " (label) {title}"
A submenu, up to its own
.BR [end] .
.TP
.BI [include] " (file or directory)"
The items of another file here, or of every file in a directory (in
order, without dotfiles and backup~ files).
.TP
.B [separator]
.TP
.BI [nop] " (label)"
A label that does nothing.
.TP
.BI [style] " (label) {file}"
Switch to a style.
.TP
.BI [stylesdir] " (directory)\fR, " [stylesmenu] " {directory}"
Every style in a directory, here (files, and directories with a
.I theme.cfg
or
.IR style.cfg ).
.B [themesdir]
and
.B [themesmenu]
are the same.
.TP
.BI [wallpapers] " (directory) {command}"
Every file of a directory, here, each running
.I "command file"
(also
.B [wallpapermenu]
and
.BR [rootcommands] ).
Without a command, or with an X11 setter such as Fluxbox's
.BR fbsetbg ,
the file becomes the wallpaper
.RB ( SetWallpaper ).
.TP
.BI [workspaces] " (label)"
The workspaces, to switch to, add or remove one.
.TP
.BI [icons] " (label)"
The iconified windows.
.TP
.BI [config] " (label)"
Some settings to change.
.TP
.BI [reconfig] " (label)"
Read the configuration again (Reload Config).
.TP
.BI [restart] " (label)"
The same, since a compositor can't restart under its windows.
.TP
.BI [exit] " (label)"
Quit.
.TP
.BI [macrocmd] " (label) {{command} {command} ...}"
.TP
.BI [ Command "] (label) {arguments}"
Any other tag is a command of
.BR fluxland-keys (5)
with the
.I arguments
after it:
.B "[MaximizeWindow] (Maximize)"
or
.BR "[SetStyle] (Bloe) {~/.fluxbox/styles/Bloe}" .
fluxland's
.BI [command] " (label) {command}"
takes any command.
.TP
.BI [encoding] " {charset}\fR ... " [endencoding]
The labels between are in another character set, such as
.BR ISO-8859-1 ;
this carries into submenus and included files.
.PP
A label left out takes a default for the tag.
.SH WINDOW MENU
The window menu's items act on the window it was opened for:
.BR [shade] ,
.BR [stick] ,
.BR [maximize] ,
.BR [iconify] ,
.BR [raise] ,
.BR [lower] ,
.B [close]
and
.B [kill]
.RB ( [killwindow] ),
.B [sendto]
(the workspaces),
.B [layer]
(Fluxbox's layers),
.B [alpha]
(its opacity),
.B [extramenus]
(Remember...: a toggle for each of the window's settings Fluxbox can
keep in
.BR fluxland-apps (5)
\(em its workspace, jumping there, head, dimensions, position, sticky,
decorations, shaded, minimized, maximized, fullscreen, transparency,
layer and saving on close \(em written there at once),
and
.B [settitledialog]
(a dialog to type its title in).
.B [commanddialog]
in any menu opens the dialog of
.BR CommandDialog .
.SH USING MENUS
Hovering over a submenu opens it (after
.BR session.screen0.menuDelay ),
and so does pressing a button on it.
An item runs when the button is let go over it, as Fluxbox's do:
.B [maximize]
maximizes with the left button, up and down with the middle one and
across with the right one, and a workspace of
.B [sendto]
with the middle button takes you along.
The menu closes, unless Control is held or the item is a setting or
shade, stick, iconify or maximize, which leave it open to show what
they did.
A menu is moved by dragging its title, and closed by right-clicking
it.
Typing searches the menu for an item whose label starts with what was
typed
.RB ( session.menuSearch :
.BR itemstart ,
the default;
.B somewhere
to search the whole label;
.B nowhere
to turn it off); Backspace edits what was typed.
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down
Select the item above or below.
.TP
.BR Right ", " Return
Open the submenu, or run the item.
.TP
.B Left
Back to the menu above.
.TP
.B Escape
Close the menus.
.PP
With
.B session.menuSearch: nowhere ,
.BR h ", " j ", " k ", " l
move as the arrow keys do.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
[begin] (fluxland)
  [exec] (Terminal) {foot} <~/.icons/terminal.png>
  [exec] (Web Browser) {firefox}
  [separator]
  [submenu] (Styles) {Choose a style}
    [stylesdir] (~/.fluxbox/styles)
    [stylesdir] (/usr/share/fluxland/styles)
  [end]
  [submenu] (Backgrounds)
    [wallpapers] (~/Pictures/Wallpapers)
  [end]
  [workspaces] (Workspaces)
  [include] (~/.config/fluxland/menu.d)
  [separator]
  [config] (Configuration)
  [reconfig] (Reload Config)
  [exit] (Exit)
[end]
.fi
.RE
.SH COMPATIBILITY
fluxland 1.x put
.B [wallpapers]
and
.B [stylesmenu]
in submenus of their own (with the directory in braces); they are now
listed in place, as in Fluxbox.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fluxland (1),
.BR fluxland-keys (5),
.BR fluxland-apps (5),
.BR fluxland-init (5)
